  "title": "Great Temple of Hera",
  "provenance": "Pleiades",
  "placeTypeURIs": [
    "https://pleiades.stoa.org/vocabularies/place-types/temple-2"
  ],
  "details": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>The Great Temple of Hera (or Polycrates temple) is the third temple to Hera at the Samian Heraion. Constructed by the tyrant Polycrates between 540 and 530 BCE, the temple measured 55.16 m x 108.63 m. The Ionic temple was built in a peristyle of at least 155, 20 m columns, which makes it one of the largest Greek temples built. The temple served as the hub for the cult of the Samian Hera and housed the <em>xoanon</em> \u2014 wooden cult statue \u2014 of Hera. During the Byzantine period, the temple was extensively quarried.</span></p>",
  "review_state": "published",
